From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Jerrod <jerrod.uno@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 20 Oct 2026 01:15:00 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] system: --xex_patch, apply an XEX patch from a given guest path

The runtime applies default.xexp from next to default.xex. The Crackdown
title-update build needs Title Update #6 applied while the disc build,
which shares the game folder, must not see it. --xex_patch names the
patch's guest path instead (e.g. update:\default.xexp with
--update_data_root pointing at the unpacked update); a missing file fails
the load. The patch file's own load skips the lookup (it used to find no
sibling; with an override it would recurse). Unset, nothing changes.

Host paths only; no guest code touched. Checked on the PC 2026-10-20:
crackdown_tu with the disc game folder and title-update\ next to the exe
logs "XEX patch applied successfully: 0.0.0.1 -> 0.0.6.1", mounts both
DLC packs and plays Keys to the City (62.0 fps avg over 30 s).
---
diff --git a/src/system/user_module.cpp b/src/system/user_module.cpp
index 171546f..e2931ee 100644
--- a/src/system/user_module.cpp
+++ b/src/system/user_module.cpp
@@ -24,0 +25,5 @@
+#include <rex/string/utf8.h>
+
+REXCVAR_DEFINE_STRING(xex_patch, "", "Runtime",
+                      "Guest path of the XEX patch (.xexp) to apply to the main module, e.g. "
+                      "update:\\default.xexp; empty = default.xexp next to the XEX");
@@ -105,2 +110,16 @@ X_STATUS UserModule::LoadFromFile(const std::string_view path) {
-  // Search for sibling XEX patch file
-  auto patch_entry = kernel_state_->file_system()->ResolvePath(path_ + "p");
+  // Search for sibling XEX patch file, or the one --xex_patch names (a guest
+  // path such as update:\default.xexp) so a title update can live outside the
+  // game folder that an unpatched build also reads.
+  // The patch itself loads through here too; it never gets a patch.
+  const bool is_patch_file =
+      path_.size() >= 5 && rex::string::utf8_lower_ascii(path_.substr(path_.size() - 5)) == ".xexp";
+  if (is_patch_file) {
+    return LoadXexContinue();
+  }
+  const std::string& patch_override = REXCVAR_GET(xex_patch);
+  auto patch_entry = kernel_state_->file_system()->ResolvePath(
+      patch_override.empty() ? path_ + "p" : patch_override);
+  if (!patch_entry && !patch_override.empty()) {
+    REXSYS_ERROR("--xex_patch {} not found", patch_override);
+    return X_STATUS_UNSUCCESSFUL;
+  }
